      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like to avoid touching so much code given that this isn\u0027t for upstream. Some alternatives are:\n\n1. Probe the PSCI features directly from EL2, e.g. by calling a `psci_features_init()` function from `__pkvm_init_finalise()` which could query the features and stash the value somewhere in `psci-relay.c`\n\n2. Probe for `PSCI_MEM_PROTECT` at EL1 in `init_psci_relay()` and flip a static key which is used at EL2 in `psci_mem_protect)`\n\n3. Have a cmdline option along the lines of `kvm-arm.psci_mem_protect\u003don|off|auto` to either force it on, don\u0027t touch it or have the current toggling behaviour\n\n4. Add a hypervisor module callback for the mem_protect logic and only call PSCI if nothing has been registered by a module.\n\nWDYT?",
